Data-plane checks also look clean. End-to-end host reachability across the network is normal: pc0 (20.1.1.10) ↔ pc12 (120.1.1.10) ping succeeds 0% loss with ~2.8–2.9 ms RTT. Multiple targeted pings to R7 from different parts of the network (r3, r4, r5, r8) all succeed with 0% loss and low RTTs, indicating traffic “through the middle” is passing.

Localization: the interconnect between R6 eth2 (Y) and R7 eth0 (Y) is up and exchanging routes; no interface or daemon faults observed. Mechanism: with OSPF adjacencies Full and routing tables consistent, forwarding works as expected.

Root cause: No ongoing fault; likely a transient flap or false alert.

Corrective fix: None required. Recommend reviewing FRR logs for any brief overnight OSPF flaps and adding hysteresis/dampening to the monitoring alerts to avoid future false positives. 
